// Conquord subject: src/fiat2/eval/HA_LookinFunctions.v
//
// The list is an INPUT -- the component is handed its device at
// construction and only reads it -- so there is no op, which in Cozy's
// terms is a spec with queries and no updates.  That is the whole subject:
// two membership tests and nothing else, and what the programmer wrote by
// hand is a set of the names.
//
// Encoding decision: the subject's two reads differ only in whether the
// probed name is a literal, which matters to the rewriting (one is an N+1
// inside a loop over constants) and not to a synthesizer, so both appear
// here as the one parameterised query.
Lookin:

    type Func = { name : String }

    state functions : Bag<Func>

    query hasFunction(n : String)
        exists [f | f <- functions, f.name == n]
